{% extends "base.html.j2" %}
{% block title %}Harness · Loom{% endblock %}
{% block description %}The open-source Loom Benchmark Lab: run it against a simulated GPU in minutes, or reproduce a published result.{% endblock %}
{% block content %}
<header class="page-head">
<h1>The harness</h1>
<p class="lede">Every number on this site comes from the Loom Benchmark Lab, open source under Apache-2.0. Run it without a GPU against a simulated one, or rerun any published result.</p>
<p><a class="button" href="{{ config.repo }}">Source on GitHub</a></p>
</header>

<section aria-labelledby="quickstart">
<h2 id="quickstart">Quickstart with the mock backend</h2>
<p>The mock is an OpenAI-compatible streaming server that simulates a batching GPU: queueing, prefill and decode costs, prefix caching and Prometheus metrics. You need Python 3.12+ and <code>uv</code>; no GPU.</p>
<ol class="steps">
<li>
<p>Clone the repository and install the workspace.</p>
<pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>git clone {{ config.repo }}.git
cd loom
uv sync</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<p>Run the tests. No GPU needed; tests that need Postgres are skipped unless <code>LOOM_TEST_DATABASE_URL</code> is set.</p>
<pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>uv run pytest</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<p>Start the mock and send it a streaming request.</p>
<pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>uv run python -m loom_bench.mock --port 8000

curl -N http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/chat/completions \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"model": "mock-model", "stream": true,
       "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Hello"}]}'</code></pre>
</li>
<li>
<p>Explore the command line.</p>
<pre class="code" tabindex="0"><code>uv run bench --help</code></pre>
</li>
</ol>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="reproduce">
<h2 id="reproduce">Reproducing a published result</h2>
<ul class="short">
<li>Each config on a model page lists its runs, links each run's provenance file, and gives a <code>bench reproduce &lt;run id&gt;</code> command.</li>
<li>The provenance records everything the run depended on: the git commit, engine version and image digest, model revision, GPU, CUDA and driver versions, cloud, region and market, workload profile and dataset, load mode and seed.</li>
<li>Reproducing reruns that configuration and reports whether the new numbers are within normal run-to-run variance of the original.</li>
<li>Cloud runs need your own cloud account and pay its prices.</li>
</ul>
</section>

<section aria-labelledby="layout">
<h2 id="layout">What is in the repository</h2>
<dl class="defs compact">
<dt><a href="{{ config.repo }}/tree/main/bench"><code>bench/</code></a></dt><dd>The Benchmark Lab: load generator, metrics, SLO and goodput search, cost, results store, reports and this site.</dd>
<dt><a href="{{ registry_url }}"><code>config/models.yaml</code></a></dt><dd>The model registry: pinned weights revision, digest-pinned engine image, hardware, parallelism and planned price for every model.</dd>
<dt><a href="{{ config.repo }}/blob/main/bench/prices.yaml"><code>bench/prices.yaml</code></a></dt><dd>Cloud prices with sources and check dates.</dd>
<dt><a href="{{ config.repo }}/blob/main/bench/competitors.yaml"><code>bench/competitors.yaml</code></a></dt><dd>Other providers' public list prices with sources and check dates.</dd>
<dt><a href="{{ config.repo }}/tree/main/bench/workloads"><code>bench/workloads/</code></a></dt><dd>Workload profiles: fixed input/output shapes, chat, shared prefix, long-context retrieval, code completion, long generation and trace replay.</dd>
<dt><a href="{{ config.repo }}/tree/main/site/data"><code>site/data/</code></a></dt><dd>The results snapshot this site is built from.</dd>
</dl>
</section>
{% endblock %}
